# Futrob architecture

Canonical sources: `docs/architecture/overview.md`, `docs/architecture/module-boundaries.md`, `docs/architecture/dependency-graph.md`, relevant ADRs (including 0010, 0013 and 0015), and [futrob-hexagonal-module](../skills/futrob-hexagonal-module/SKILL.md).

## Shape

- Deployable Must: `apps/web` on Cloudflare Workers.
- API de producto: `apps/api` (Hono/Node, Railway, Postgres y egress EA). Auth: `apps/auth` (Better Auth Worker). Mobile: `apps/mobile` (Expo).
- Business logic: `packages/<context>/` (`@futrob/<bc>`) = `domain` / `application` / ports.
- App slice: `apps/web/src/modules/<context>/` = `adapters` / `server` / `presentation` + facade `index.ts`.
- Product composition in `apps/api/src/di/`; web BFF/Workers infrastructure in `apps/web/src/{bootstrap,config,context}/`.
- Shared: `@futrob/shared-kernel` + `apps/web/src/shared/` (infra web; domain reexports kernel).
- Queue/Cron thin handlers: `apps/web/src/workers/`.
- Native UI uses `@futrob/sdk` and shared tokens; it does not import BC implementations or web render trees.

MVP BCs: `identity`, `organizations`, `competitions`, `teams`, `scheduling`, `game-data`, `results`, `statistics`, `analytics`, `notifications`, `public-portal`.

## Dependency direction

```text
web/mobile UI → web BFF → SDK → apps/api HTTP → @futrob/<bc> application → domain/ports
apps/api DI → product adapters (Postgres / EA HTTP)
```

- Domain: no React, Zod, D1, fetch, Wrangler env, Sentry.
- Application: no concrete adapters.
- Package `index.ts`: no adapters, schemas DB, mappers, HTTP clients.
- Cross-module: package public API, bridges on ports, or outbox events — never foreign adapters/tables.

## Separation

```text
scheduling → when / how many
game-data  → provider observations (EA is an adapter)
results    → official selection / confirmation / disputes
statistics → standings / rankings from approved results only
analytics  → premium interpretation
```

## Persistence and runtime

- Product persistence: Postgres in apps/api. Auth/actors and BFF rate limits: shared D1, migration history in apps/auth. Blobs: R2. Provider jobs: Queues + Cron in web calling the API.
- Tenancy: application-scoped `organizationId` in adapters (no Postgres RLS).
- Better Auth owns sessions; the API resolves Futrob capabilities from the relevant organization, competition and roster context. Presentation uses `EffectiveAccess` and the existing `can` / `useCan` / `useCapabilities` helpers, with BC permission constants. Backend use cases enforce access.
- The API currently uses a no-op domain event publisher and transactionally composes official-result/statistics updates. Inspect wiring before relying on outbox delivery; provider sync Queues/Cron have a separate implemented path.

## Imports and doc links

- TypeScript in web: prefer `@futrob/<bc>` for domain/application; `@/` for app-local paths (`apps/web/src/*`). Do not use `../` parent-relative imports across packages.
- Markdown in `docs/` and `product/`: link with repo-root absolute paths (`/docs/...`, `/product/...`), not `../`.
